			"content": "<p><a href=\"https://mstdn.social/@mattwilcox\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@mattwilcox@mstdn.social</a><span> </span><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@zachleat@fediverse.zachleat.com</a><span> <br><br>FSA provider disputed one of my claims. Couldn't just wire them the money to get my account reactivated, I had to mail them a cheque.<br><br>Similarly, with Zelle (et. al.) deactivating accounts that don't have \"real\" cellphone numbers associated with them, I'm no longer able to use money-transfer apps for personal expenses. So, if non-businesses need money from me, it's gonna have to be in the form of cheque.</span></p>",
