			"date": "2025-06-20T22:36:00.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> It wasn’t cheap, you had to pay to send. They were mostly business to business IIRC, so not really a plaything. You could see the senders number. And, maybe crucially, you couldn’t see the recipient’s reaction, unlike social media trolling these days. However, mates would send each other “memes” or jokes with them. I remember seeing them on my dad’s office wall.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
